{"data":{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.22752862","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.5281/zenodo.22752862","prefix":"10.5281","suffix":"zenodo.22752862","identifiers":[{"identifier":"oai:zenodo.org:22752862","identifierType":"oai"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"alternateIdentifierType":"oai","alternateIdentifier":"oai:zenodo.org:22752862"}],"creators":[{"name":"Jayadevan, Achyuth","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Achyuth","familyName":"Jayadevan","affiliation":["Manipal Institute of Technology, MAHE"],"nameIdentifiers":[{"nameIdentifier":"0009-0008-8745-4078","nameIdentifierScheme":"ORCID"}]}],"titles":[{"title":"Bounded-index nilpotent subgroups of rational linear groups with finitely many automorphism orbits"}],"publisher":"Zenodo","container":{},"publicationYear":2026,"subjects":[],"contributors":[],"dates":[{"date":"2026-09-14","dateType":"Issued"}],"language":"en","types":{"ris":"GEN","bibtex":"misc","citeproc":"article","schemaOrg":"CreativeWork","resourceType":"","resourceTypeGeneral":"Preprint"},"relatedIdentifiers":[{"relationType":"IsVersionOf","relatedIdentifier":"10.5281/zenodo.22752861","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"}],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":[],"formats":[],"version":"1.0.0","rightsList":[{"rights":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","rightsUri":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode","schemeUri":"https://spdx.org/licenses/","rightsIdentifier":"cc-by-4.0","rightsIdentifierScheme":"SPDX"},{"rights":"Copyright © 2026 Achyuth Jayadevan.","rightsUri":"http://rightsstatements.org/vocab/InC/1.0/"}],"descriptions":[{"description":"Let \\(G\\leq\\operatorname{GL}_n(\\mathbb Q)\\) have finitely many orbits under its full abstract automorphism group, and put \\(d=\\dim_{\\mathbb Q}\\operatorname{span}_{\\mathbb Q}G\\). We prove that \\(G\\) has a torsion-free normal subgroup \\(U\\) satisfying \\[ \\gamma_n(U)=1,\\qquad [G:U]\\leq(2n+1)^d\\leq(2n+1)^{n^2}. \\] Thus \\(G\\) is virtually nilpotent, answering Kourovka Problem 21.40 affirmatively. More generally, if the trace set \\(T=\\{\\operatorname{tr}(g):g\\in G\\}\\) is finite, the same subgroup satisfies \\([G:U]\\leq |T|^d\\). The proof combines bounded-degree roots of algebraic numbers with the trace radical of the rational matrix algebra generated by \\(G\\). Restriction of scalars gives corresponding bounds over number fields.","descriptionType":"Abstract"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"xml":"","url":"https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22752862","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":0,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"api","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"viewsOverTime":[],"downloadCount":0,"downloadsOverTime":[],"referenceCount":0,"citationCount":0,"citationsOverTime":[],"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":0,"versionOfCount":1,"created":"2026-09-14T14:43:08.000Z","registered":"2026-09-14T14:43:08.000Z","published":"2026","updated":"2026-09-14T14:43:08.000Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"data":{"id":"cern.zenodo","type":"clients"}},"provider":{"data":{"id":"cern","type":"providers"}},"media":{"data":{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.22752862","type":"media"}},"references":{"data":[]},"citations":{"data":[]},"parts":{"data":[]},"partOf":{"data":[]},"versions":{"data":[]},"versionOf":{"data":[{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.22752861","type":"dois"}]}}}}